The first fix is not enough: DP register-shift words have bit4=1 and are still routed to media by the op2 tests. Verified with the ARM corpus: e1a01fa1 (lsr r1,r1,#31), e1a011a2 (lsr r2,r2,#3), e1a011c0 (lsl r0,r0,#3), e1a002a0 (lsl r0,r0,#5), e1a00080 (lsl r0,r0,#1) all stop UNDEF at their first occurrence. My tmp-patched core with the following exact change runs k_absdiff/k_add64/... correctly (remaining stops are only genuinely missing V12/V17 instructions):

  case 0:
      op = (insn >> 20) & 0x1Fu;
      if ((op & 0x10u) != 0) {
          op2 = (insn >> 4) & 0xFu;
          hi = op & 0xFu;
          /* extra load/store: bit4 AND bit7, not just bit4 */
          if (hi >= 8u && (insn & 0x90u) == 0x90u)
              return n2a32_arm_mem;
          /* QADD/QSUB/SMLAxy/SMULxy only when bits[27:23] == 00010; a DP word
             such as MOV/LSR r1,r1,#31 has bits[27:23] == 00011 and bit4 == 1. */
          if (((insn >> 23) & 0x1Fu) == 0x02u) {
              if (op2 == 5u) return n2a32_arm_media;
              if (op2 == 8u || op2 == 0xAu || op2 == 0xCu || op2 == 0xEu)
                  return n2a32_arm_media;
          }
          if ((insn & 0x0FF000F0u) == 0x01200070u) return n2a32_arm_misc;
          if (hi == 2u && ...) return n2a32_arm_misc;
          return n2a32_arm_dp;
      }
      return n2a32_arm_dp;

QADD e1020051, QSUB e1253054, SMLABB e1069887, BKPT e1200071, BX e12fff13 all have bits[27:23]==2, so their routing is unchanged. Repro: build diffrun against your core (my /tmp/n2hw-T01/exp2/run0/diffrun2) and run k_absdiff: with the old line it stops at e1a01fa1; with the patch it returns normally. Only the bit24 branch changes.
